  "text": "Recipe: Lauki Leaves Patra\nCreator: Manisha Deora\nCategory: Snack\nIngredients: lauki leaves (bottle gourd leaves), chickpea flour, water, spices (of your choice), garlic, ginger, chili, mustard seeds, sesame seeds, curry leaves, collard greens, dino kale\nCooking methods: steam, saute, air-fry\nInstructions: (1) Smear lauki leaves (bottle gourd leaves) with thick besan paste made from chickpea flour mixed with water, spices of your choice and garlic/ginger/chili paste. Fold them and roll them up as shown in pic. (2) Steam for 10 to 15 minutes. Keep flipping & checking until the leaves are cooked. (3) Chop them into pieces as shown in pic when warm enough to handle. Prepare some Dry Tadka by dry saut\u00e9ing mustard seeds, sesame seeds & curry leaves. Sprinkle Dry Tadka on the steamed & cut Patras or slowly rotate cut Patras in the pan with Dry Tadka. (4) Air fry at 370 C. Keep checking & flipping every 3-4 minutes.\nNotes: A recipe with BEANS (chickpea flour), LEAFY GREENS (lauki leaves), HERBS & SPICES (various). TIP: We may make these Patra with other leafy greens like collard greens & dino kale too.",
